piggybank.py: (1) Origin must now EXACTLY equal the serving origin http://127.0.0.1:<bound port> — the startswith prefix check accepted http://127.0.0.1.evil.example, wrong ports, and trailing-garbage origins; (2) mutation guard: Transfer-Encoding refused, Content-Length must parse and equal 0, form-family Content-Types (application/x-www-form-urlencoded, multipart/*) refused — refresh takes no input, so every classic HTML-form CSRF carrier is refused even empty; (3) send_response override emits Content-Security-Policy (strict 'self'; index.html carries only external /app.js and /styles.css — verified), X-Content-Type-Options nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY, Referrer-Policy no-referrer on EVERY response including send_error paths (403/404 included).

tests/test_m1_hardening.py NEW: 20 tests across exact-origin (6), mutation guard incl. raw-socket chunked (5), security headers on index/app.js/summary/token/200/403/404 (7), token lifecycle stable-within-process + differs-across-processes (2). tests/test_csrf_contract.py: post helper now sends data=None — faithful to the browser's bodiless fetch(); the former data=b'' made urllib invent a form Content-Type, which the new guard rightly refuses.

Fail-before (B1-2 state): 14/20 hardening tests FAIL. Pass-after: 26/26 (hardening + B1-2 contract) and 31/31 full tokencenter discover, evidence lane untouched.

